a Sources\n\n| Data Point | NexLev Tool Used | Status |\n|-----------|-----------------|--------|\n| Channel profile | `youtube_channel_about` | ✅ |\n| RPM / Revenue / Demographics | `get_geography_revenue` | ✅ |\n| Monetization check | `check_channel_monetization` | ✅/❌ |\n```\n\n## Rate Limit Awareness\n\nNexLev FREE plan limits (per 24 hours):\n- `youtube_channel_about`: 50 calls/day\n- `get_geography_revenue`: **5 calls/day** (most limited!)\n- `check_channel_monetization`: 5 calls/day\n- `youtube_channel_videos`: 50 calls/day\n\nIf rate limited on `get_geography_revenue`, note it in the report and estimate using similar channels' data from the same niche.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- **Connection timeout**: Retry once. NexLev servers occasionally drop.\n- **\"Proactive token refresh failed\"**: This is NORMAL. Ignore these warnings.\n- **Auth errors**: Tell user to run `nexlev_kill_stale.py` and retry.\n- **Unicode errors on Windows**: Use `$env:PYTHONIOENCODING='utf-8'` before Python calls.\n\n## Key Insights to Always Include\n\nAfter generating the raw data report, add contextual analysis:\n\n1. **Growth trajectory**: Is current monthly > lifetime average? (growing) or < (declining)?\n2. **RPM vs category**: Is channel RPM above or below category average? Why?\n3. **Shorts impact**: If MIXED type, highlight how Shorts drag down effective RPM\n4. **Geographic RPM drag**: High India/SEA traffic = lower RPM vs category\n5. **Per-video efficiency**: Revenue per video compared to other channels\n6. **Notable patterns**: TTS voice, faceless, high upload frequency, etc.\n","Description":"YouTube Channel Audit skill - reusable template for NexLev-powered channel analysis","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\youtube-channel-audit\\SKILL.md","toolAction":"Creating skill","toolSummary":"Channel audit skill"}}]}
